      "text": "Given that \\( g(f(x)) = 3x + 4 \\), we start by substituting the expression for \\( f(x) \\) into \\( g \\).\n\nFirst, recall that \\( f(x) = ax + b \\). Thus,\n\\[\ng(f(x)) = g(ax + b) = 2(ax + b) - 5 = 2ax + 2b - 5.\n\\]\nWe know this expression must be equal to \\( 3x + 4 \\), so we equate the resulting expressions:\n\\[\n2ax + 2b - 5 = 3x + 4.\n\\]\nBy comparing coefficients of \\( x \\) and the constant terms on both sides, we can deduce:\n\\[\n2a = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2b - 5 = 4.\n\\]\nSolving the first equation for \\( a \\):\n\\[\n2a = 3 \\implies a = \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\nSolving the second equation for \\( b \\):\n\\[\n2b - 5 = 4 \\implies 2b = 9 \\implies b = \\frac{9}{2}.\n\\]\nFinally, calculate \\( a + b \\):\n\\[\na + b = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{9}{2} = \\frac{3 + 9}{2} = \\frac{12}{2} = 6.\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\( a + b \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}.\n\\]",
